  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1241 PM EST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nA large high pressure ridge will dominate the weather pattern for\nthe next several days as it slowly drifts east across the \nOH Valley and Appalachians. Dry conditions will continue through\nthe week, with temperatures trending slightly upward each day as \nthe ridge moves to the Mid Atlantic region and brings a broad \nsoutherly flow around the middle of the week. Highs will be in the\n65 to 70 range by the weekend. Skies will be mostly sunny each \nday, but we may see an uptick in cloud cover Thursday/Friday on \nthe northern side of a low pressure system over the Gulf. This low\ngets picked up by a mid-latitude shortwave trough over the\nweekend, but right now it appears to track well to our east, with\nprecip staying across GA and the Carolinas. The shortwave trough\npassage over the weekend looks pretty benign and unlikely to\nproduce any precip worth mentioning at this point.",
